"""batchalign-gui src-tauri — Tauri v2 desktop app (Path A wrapper).

Same boundary as chatter-gui:
  - Bazel: lists the Bazel-built sidecar and the intra-workspace Rust
    crates this app depends on (none currently, since the GUI talks to
    the daemon over HTTP rather than linking the engine), and stages
    the sidecar binary with the right target-triple suffix.
  - Cargo: `cargo tauri build` resolves Cargo.toml deps and drives the
    full end-to-end bundle (Vite SPA → cargo rustc → platform bundler).

The sidecar daemon (//python/batchalign:sidecar) is the key new input.
The `env = { SIDECAR_PATH: ... }` attribute passes the runfile path of
that target into bundle.sh, which stages it under src-tauri/binaries/
before invoking cargo tauri build.
"""

load("@rules_shell//shell:sh_binary.bzl", "sh_binary")

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

# Both `bundle` and `dev` declare //python/batchalign:sidecar as data.
# Bazel materializes the sidecar's sh_binary launcher into our runfiles
# tree; the wrapper scripts then execute that launcher (escape-path
# build via pyapp_build.sh) before staging the produced sidecar binary
# under src-tauri/binaries/. This gives `bazel run` / `just batchalign::
# gui::{build,dev}` a single-shot contract: build, stage, and run with
# no "build it first" prerequisites.

sh_binary(
    name = "bundle",
    srcs = ["//bazel/batchalign-tauri:bundle.sh"],
    data = [
        "//apps/batchalign/batchalign-gui:frontend_sources",
        "//python/batchalign:sidecar",
    ],
    env = {
        "SIDECAR_PATH": "$(rootpath //python/batchalign:sidecar)",
    },
)

sh_binary(
    name = "dev",
    srcs = ["//bazel/batchalign-tauri:dev.sh"],
    data = [
        "//apps/batchalign/batchalign-gui:frontend_sources",
        "//python/batchalign:sidecar",
    ],
    env = {
        "SIDECAR_PATH": "$(rootpath //python/batchalign:sidecar)",
    },
)
